From: Emerald Tablet downstream
Subject: [PATCH 0013] Keep two-finger cancel available in Pencil mode

Pencil mode makes ordinary finger touches navigation-only so they cannot place
or select anything.  That filter also disabled the documented two-finger tap
secondary action, leaving users dependent on a stationary Pencil hold or the
Pencil side gesture to cancel a selected construction tool.

A two-finger tap is already handled only as a secondary/cancel action.  Allow
that deliberate gesture in Pencil mode while preserving the existing ban on
ordinary finger clicks.

---
 src/input/touch.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/input/touch.cpp b/src/input/touch.cpp
index 34e7d1e..1593899 100644
--- a/src/input/touch.cpp
+++ b/src/input/touch.cpp
@@ -84,7 +84,6 @@ int touch_was_two_finger_tap(void) {
     const touch_t *first = get_earliest_touch();
     const touch_t *last = get_latest_touch();
-    if (!last->in_use || touch_is_navigation_only(first) || touch_is_navigation_only(last)
-        || last->start_time - first->start_time >= CLICK_TIME
+    if (!last->in_use || last->start_time - first->start_time >= CLICK_TIME
         || first->has_moved || last->has_moved
         || first->long_press_handled || last->long_press_handled) {
         return 0;
-- 
